{"actor": "opencode", "data": {"refs": ["EXPERIMENTS/005-knitting-bounded-search/bounded.py"], "summary": "rejected the interrupted draft bounded.py: its per-neighbourhood candidates are cross-multiplied, so the enumerated combination count equals the oracle's 2^|errors| on every 004 case (measured), making 'all_bounded_optimal=true' a tautology of the decomposition rather than evidence; replacing it with a planner that takes each neighbourhood's minimum and charges the union of releases once, plus a chunk-cap and beam sweep that makes the boundedness and the failure boundary measurable"}, "host": "instance-20260717-0947", "kind": "decision", "schema": "origin.session.event/1", "seq": 4, "session": "2026-10-03-023-t-0011-bounded-neighbourhood-knitting-pl", "ts": "2026-10-03T19:09:59+00:00"}
